 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the civil practice law and rules, in relation to a referee's\ncompensation",
    "basePrintNo": "S8351",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8351-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §8003, CPLR",
    "lawSection": "Civil Practice Law and Rules",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8351\n\nSPONSOR: GOLDEN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the civil practice law and rules, in\nrelation to a referee's compensation\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo amend the civil practice law and rules section 8003 regarding refer-\nees fees.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would amend the civil practice law and rules regarding referee\nrules. Section 8003(a) would now allow a referee to be entitled, for\neach day spent in the business of the reference, to three hundred fifty\ndollars unless a different compensation is fixed by the court or by the\nconsent in writing of all parties not in default for failure to appear\nor please. Section 8003(b) now increases a referee's compensation,\nincluding commissions, upon a sale pursuant to a judgement in any action\nwhich cannot exceed seven hundred fifty dollars, unless the property\nsold for fifty thousand dollars or more, in which event the referee may\nreceive such additional compensation as to the court may seem proper.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nGenerally, a referee is entitled, for each day spent in the business of\nreference, to fifty dollars unless a different compensation is fixed by\nthe courts or by consent in writing of all parties not in default for\nfailure to appear or plead. It has been increasingly difficult to\nattract lawyers to take on such appointments because of the low prices.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n1997: S.2293-A - Referred to Codes\n1996: S.7527 - Referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
